Town C: "When the full moon occurs in Gemini, start counting your steps. On the fifth day of the moon's journey, you will commence the operation." This means each town could have a slightly different timetable based on the moonâ€™s phases, but all events are still in sync on a larger scale. 
3. Maximizing the Impact of the Massacre: By choosing specific celestial events, Mithridates could ensure that the timing of the massacre is perfectly synchronized in terms of the chaos it would generate. The shockwaves from the massacre in the key cities might not even hit all towns simultaneously, but by having the celestial events act as markers, each locationâ€™s response will feel part of a larger, orchestrated plan.
