Thematic Power of the Celestial Manipulation
Thereâ€™s a larger thematic element at play here: the idea that history, fate, and even people's lives can be determined by a higher order (symbolized by the stars, celestial events, etc.). Mithridates isnâ€™t just using tactics and military prowess; he's using the cosmos itself to create his reality. This makes him appear both god-like and monstrous, as he manipulates events on a cosmic scale.
